   144	All **82** transformed polynomials retained negative coefficients; **zero** cells were recovered. The run took 0.621 seconds, and `newton/manifest.json` binds every attempted source polynomial by SHA-256. This failed sufficient test does not refute positivity or injectivity. No unused Newton-certificate acceptance branch remains in the independent checker.
   145	
   146	## Reproducibility, bounds, and storage
   147	
   148	All commands are recorded exactly in `commands.txt`; producer input specifications record source hashes, parameter domains, dependency receipt hashes, and computational bounds. All mathematical runs were serial, with one process and FLINT configured for one thread.
   149	
   150	Observed runtimes:
   151	
   152	| Run | Seconds |
   153	|---|---:|
   154	| Corrected three-degree campaign, total | 2508.007 |
   155	| Initial `322` stage | 107.801 |
   156	| `422` stage | 1200.123 |
   157	| `332` stage | 1200.019 |
   158	| Longer ordinary Bareiss attempt, timed out | 603.661 |
   159	| Successful row-content `322` supplement | 118.566 |
   160	| Failed falling-factorial positivity pass | 0.621 |
   161	
   162	The ordinary campaign used 30 seconds per selected minor, 1,200 seconds per degree, at most three deterministic row-order choices, and a 250,000-monomial intermediate-entry cap. Signal delivery can occur after a running FLINT operation returns, explaining small deadline overruns. The row-content supplement used a 300-second limit and the same term cap.
   163	
   164	An initial run stopped because FLINT exponent objects were not directly JSON serializable. The fix was explicit integer conversion. `initial-failure.json` and the original partial output directory preserve that failure; the corrected campaign used `candidates/` and overwrote nothing. The partial initial gzip is not an acceptance certificate.
   165	
   166	At the recorded storage snapshot, this evidence directory occupied **12,724 KiB**, and the entire target occupied **38,548 KiB**, comfortably below the shared storage constraints. The final small report and summary files were added after that snapshot.
