   400	
   401	### 5.1 The theorem and its full proof
   402	
   403	**Theorem.** Fix a node `i`, let `J` be its complement, and suppose
   404	
   405	\[
   406	B=A_J\text{ is invertible},\qquad B^{-1}\ge0
   407	\]
   408	
   409	entrywise. Define
   410	
   411	\[
   412	r=-B^{-1}a_{Ji}\ge0,\qquad C_i=1+\sum_{j\in J}r_j.
   413	\tag{5.1}
   414	\]
   415	
   416	Suppose `I_alpha=K_alpha` has been established for **every** positive degree of total height at most `H`. If an integer `k>=0` satisfies
   417	
   418	\[
   419	\lfloor C_i k\rfloor\le H,
   420	\tag{5.2}
   421	\]
   422	
   423	then equality holds for every positive degree with `alpha_i<=k`, without a total-height restriction.
   424	
   425	**Proof.** Assume there is a defect in the band `alpha_i<=k`, and choose one of least total height **within that band**. This choice does not claim global minimality among defects outside the band.
   426	
