   428	
   429	\[
   430	A\alpha\le0.
   431	\]
   432	
   433	The rows indexed by `J` say
   434	
   435	\[
   436	B\alpha_J\le-a_{Ji}\alpha_i.
   437	\]
   438	
   439	Multiplication by the entrywise nonnegative matrix `B^{-1}` preserves these coordinatewise inequalities, giving
   440	
   441	\[
   442	\alpha_J\le r\alpha_i.
   443	\tag{5.3}
   444	\]
   445	
   446	Consequently
   447	
   448	\[
   449	\operatorname{ht}(\alpha)
   450	=\alpha_i+\sum_{j\in J}\alpha_j
   451	\le C_i\alpha_i\le C_i k.
   452	\]
   453	
   454	Since height is integral, (5.2) puts this defect at height at most `H`, contradicting the assumed certificate scope. QED.
   455	
